> ## Druid Mission: The Moonseed Grove
> 
> The Fourfold Mother asks Ekemon’s group to save the **Moonseed Grove**, where a rare tree grows seeds that can heal blighted land. Someone has built a logging camp beside it and is draining its magic.
> 
> **Villain:** **Captain Bramblehook**, a cruel treasure-hunter who wants the Moonseeds to sell to the Bone-Merchant’s agents. He is guarded by two masked rooftop scouts called **the Nightleaf Twins**: **Kite** and **Moth**.
> 
> ### The mission
> 1. Travel through the glowing forest and help Dru recognize the grove’s sick animals and corrupted plants.
> 2. Sneak into—or boldly confront—the logging camp.
> 3. Fight Captain Bramblehook and the Nightleaf Twins among rope bridges, tree platforms, and swinging lanterns.
> 4. Stop Bramblehook from escaping with the Moonseed chest.
> 
> ### Encounter
> - **Captain Bramblehook:** use a Bandit Captain-style enemy, with a thorn-whip instead of a sword.
> - **Kite and Moth:** use nimble ninja-style scouts: good at hiding, throwing sleep-smoke pellets, and leaping between trees—but not overly dangerous.
> - Add 3–4 ordinary loggers/bandits who can surrender once Bramblehook is beaten.
> 
> ### Recruiting the ninjas
> The twins are not evil. Bramblehook hired them with stolen money and threatened to expose their forest village if they quit. Once Ekemon defeats them, he can offer them a choice:
> 
> > “You fought well. You don’t have to work for a bully. Come protect my people instead.”
> 
> If he frees their village from Bramblehook’s contract—or simply returns the stolen payment—they willingly join Ekemon’s team.
> 
> ### New followers: The Nightleaf Twins
> - **Kite:** lookout, scout, rooftop messenger.
> - **Moth:** sneaky protector, trap-finder, night patrol.
> - At Titan Keep, they can guard the walls, gather rumors, or accompany Ekemon on missions where stealth matters.
> 
> The Druids reward the party with a **Moonseed Sapling** for Titan Keep: once per adventure, it can grow healing berries or reveal whether nearby water or soil has been corrupted.
