> # Moonseed Grove Mission: Scene Flow
> 
> Use DC 13 for standard checks, DC 15 for hard checks. Defeated enemies usually flee or surrender rather than die.
> 
> ## S1 — Druid Circle: The Bark Map
> The Druids explain that Captain Bramblehook is poisoning the Moonseed Grove for the Bone-Merchant.
> 
> - **Goal:** Accept the living bark-map and choose supplies.
> - **Choices:** Take healing herbs (3 healing berries, heal 1d6+2 each) or antitoxin (3 doses).
> - **Possible next scenes:** **S2 Bramblegate** or, if the party scouts through the woods successfully, **S3 Mossback Ford** with advantage on its first check.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S2 — Bramblegate
> Living thorns block the path. Glowing eyes watch from inside.
> 
> - **Checks:** Nature, Survival, or Arcana DC 13 to find the safe route; Athletics DC 15 to force an opening.
> - **Failure:** Fight 3 **Thorn Blights**. If the party uses fire, one blight begins damaged by 6 HP but the Druids dislike it.
> - **Possible next scenes:** Success or victory leads to **S3 Mossback Ford**.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S3 — Mossback Ford
> A river crosses the shell of a huge sleeping turtle. Farmer Tobin slips toward the water.
> 
> - **Checks:** Acrobatics or Athletics DC 13 to cross; DC 14 to rescue Tobin; Animal Handling DC 15 to keep Mossback asleep.
> - **Failure:** Mossback wakes, creating waves. Everyone makes a DC 13 Dexterity save or loses a turn scrambling; no battle is necessary.
> - **Reward:** If treated kindly, Mossback reveals a hidden shortcut: advantage on the first check in **S4**.
> - **Possible next scenes:** **S4 Goblin Snarewood**.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S4 — Goblin Snarewood
> Goblin trappers have captured forest animals—and possibly a young druid messenger.
> 
> - **Choices:** Sneak in, bargain, free prisoners, or fight.
> - **Battle:** 4 **Goblin Trappers**. Two begin in trees; the clearing contains 3 rope snares.
> - **Snare:** DC 13 Perception to spot; DC 13 Dexterity save if triggered or restrained. An ally can free a trapped creature with an action.
> - **Clue:** A goblin reveals Bramblehook’s men carry black sap from the grove to their camp.
> - **Possible next scenes:** **S5 Whispering Ravine**; stealthy success grants advantage on the first check there.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S5 — Whispering Ravine
> A broken rope bridge spans a misty ravine. Two shadow wolves stalk the cliffs.
> 
> - **Checks:** Repair bridge with Survival/Thieves’ Tools DC 13; cross carefully with Acrobatics DC 13; distract wolves with Animal Handling DC 14.
> - **Battle:** 2 **Shadow Wolves** attack if the party panics, attacks first, or fails two checks.
> - **Complication:** A failed crossing check leaves someone hanging from the bridge, needing an action and DC 12 Athletics check to rescue.
> - **Possible next scenes:** **S6 Moonseed Grove**.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S6 — Moonseed Grove
> The silver Moonseed Tree is being strangled by black roots. Frightened animals are trapped nearby.
> 
> - **Goal:** Save animals and cleanse the roots before the corruption spreads.
> - **Challenge:** Gain 3 successes before 2 failures: Nature, Religion, Arcana, Medicine, or Druid’s magic, DC 14.
> - **Failure:** Fight 2 **Vine Blights** and 2 **Twig Blights**, then try again with one automatic success.
> - **Success:** The Moonseed Tree gives the party a **Moonseed Charm**: once, each ally regains 2d6 HP.
> - **Clue:** Bramblehook’s camp is nearby; the Nightleaf Twins are reluctant guards, not true villains.
> - **Possible next scenes:** **S7 Logger Camp**.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S7 — Bramblehook’s Logger Camp
> Workers cut poisoned trees while guards prepare to haul away a Moonseed chest.
> 
> - **Choices:**  
>   - **Stealth:** Group Stealth DC 13; success lets the party free workers or enter the canopy fort unnoticed.  
>   - **Persuasion/Intimidation:** DC 14 convinces workers to stand aside.  
>   - **Battle:** 3 **Logger Guards** and 1 **Foreman**.
> - **Terrain:** Sawdust makes running difficult; a creature that dashes must make DC 11 Dexterity save or fall prone.
> - **Possible next scenes:** Workers reveal a climbing route to **S8**; failure or loud battle alerts Bramblehook, who gains one extra guard in S8.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## S8 — Bramblehook’s Canopy Fort
> Rope bridges and platforms surround Bramblehook’s treehouse. Kite and Moth watch from above.
> 
> - **Enemies:** Captain Bramblehook, Kite, Moth, and optionally 1 Logger Guard if alerted.
> - **Objective:** Defeat Bramblehook or force his surrender before he escapes with the Moonseed chest.
> - **Terrain:** A creature shoved from a platform falls 15 feet into nets, taking 1d6 damage and becoming restrained until freed.
> - **Recruiting the twins:** Kite and Moth surrender when Bramblehook falls below 15 HP, or if Ekemon shows them their employer lied about their village. A DC 13 Persuasion check—or returning Bramblehook’s stolen pay—makes them allies.
> - **Possible next scenes:** Return to **S1** for reward, or follow evidence of the Bone-Merchant.
> 
> # Combatants
> 
> | Creature | AC / HP | Attacks and abilities |
> |---|---:|---|
> | Thorn Blight | 13 / 22 | **Claw** +4, 1d6+2 slashing. **Needle spray** (recharge 5–6): 15-ft cone, Dex DC 12, 2d6 piercing. |
> | Goblin Trapper | 15 / 10 | **Shortbow** +4, 1d6+2 piercing; **scimitar** +4, 1d6+2. Bonus action Hide. |
> | Shadow Wolf | 14 / 18 | **Bite** +4, 1d6+2 piercing + 1d4 necrotic. Pack tactics when near another wolf. |
> | Twig Blight | 13 / 4 | **Claw** +3, 1d4+1 piercing. |
> | Vine Blight | 12 / 26 | **Constrict** +4, 2d6+2 bludgeoning; target grappled. |
> | Logger Guard | 13 / 18 | **Axe** +4, 1d8+2 slashing; **crossbow** +3, 1d8+1 piercing. |
> | Foreman | 14 / 35 | **Maul** +5, 2d6+3 bludgeoning. Once per fight, orders a guard to make one weapon attack. |
> | Captain Bramblehook | 15 / 65 | **Thorn-whip** +6, 1d6+4 piercing; pulls target 10 ft. Two attacks each turn. Once per fight: **Bramble Burst**, 15-ft radius, Dex DC 14, 3d6 piercing and difficult terrain. |
> | Kite, Nightleaf Ninja | 15 / 32 | **Shortsword** +5, 1d6+3 piercing; **shuriken** +5, 1d4+3 piercing. Bonus action Hide or Dash. |
> | Moth, Nightleaf Ninja | 15 / 32 | Same attacks as Kite. Once per fight, **smoke pellet**: 10-ft obscuring cloud for 1 round. |
> 
> Kite and Moth avoid lethal strikes and primarily target weapons, ropes, lanterns, and escape routes.
