> ## Return to the Druid Circle: The Fallen Branch
> 
> Captain Bramblehook is revealed as **Rowan Bramblehook**, once a respected druid of the Circle. He left after becoming convinced that the Druids’ patience was letting the forest die. Seeing his old friends again breaks his anger into shame.
> 
> The Druids do not celebrate his capture. They take his thorn-whip, bind him in living roots, and promise that he will face judgment—but also that he will be given a chance to heal what he harmed.
> 
> > “A branch bent by storm may yet grow toward the sun.”
> 
> ### Rewards from the Druids
> - **Moonseed Sapling:** Plant at Titan Keep. Once per adventure, it produces enough berries for the whole party to regain **$2d6$ HP each**, or it can identify nearby corruption.
> - **Bramblehook’s Reclaimed Thorn-Whip:** Ekemon may keep it, but only if he promises to use it to protect rather than exploit the wilds.  
>   - *+1 thorn-whip:* $1d6+1$ piercing, reach 15 ft; once per short rest, pull a Large-or-smaller target 10 ft on a hit.
> - **Druid Friendship:** Forest animals, druid circles, and woodland folk now recognize the party as friends of Moonseed Grove.
> - **The Nightleaf Twins:** Kite and Moth formally join Ekemon’s team after the Druids confirm that their village is safe.
> 
> ### XP
> Award **1,200 XP to each main adventurer** for the full mission: overcoming the travel dangers, saving Moonseed Grove, defeating Bramblehook’s forces, capturing him alive, and recruiting the twins.
> 
> For the lower-level companions, you can either:
> - Give **Oliver and Farmer Tobin the same 1,200 XP**—best for a heroic, fast-moving campaign; or
> - Give them **600 XP each** if you want them to remain supporting characters.
> 
> Capturing Bramblehook alive earns an additional **Druidic Favor**, not extra combat XP: later, the Circle will provide sanctuary, information, healing, or help against the Bone-Merchant.
